# Project architecture

Flutter app (`flutter_template_app`). Keep `lib/` organized by layer + feature, not `features/*/presentation`.

## Directory map

```
lib/
├── main.dart, app.dart
├── pages/              # Pages used by app_router only
├── router/             # GoRouter
├── widgets/
│   └── common/         # Shared widgets
├── providers/          # ChangeNotifiers; register in app_providers.dart
├── datasources/<feature>/
├── repositories/<feature>/
├── entities/<feature>/
├── services/<feature>/
├── core/               # Infra only: network, theme, logging, permissions
└── l10n/               # ARB + generated localizations
```

## Adding code

| What | Where |
|------|--------|
| New route page | `lib/pages/` → register in `lib/router/app_router.dart` |
| Page sub-widget | `lib/widgets/<area>/` or `lib/widgets/common/` |
| API / mock source | `lib/datasources/<feature>/` |
| Repository | `lib/repositories/<feature>/` |
| Model / enum | `lib/entities/<feature>/` |
| Business logic | `lib/services/<feature>/` |
| App state | `lib/providers/` + `app_providers.dart` |

Do not recreate `lib/features/` or nest pages under feature folders.

## Imports

- Cross-folder: `package:flutter_template_app/...` (not deep relative `../../`).
- Same subfolder widgets may use relative imports.

## Scope

- Minimal diffs; don't refactor unrelated code.
- Match existing file naming (`snake_case.dart`, `PascalCase` types).
